{"title":"ARMv7-A Bare Bones","slug":"ARMv7_A_Bare_Bones","html":"<div class=\"wk-note wk-style\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-note-label\">Wiki note</span></p>\n<p>The wiki flags this tutorial as needing more explanation of what its code does. Read the code, do not just copy it.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-note wk-warn\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-note-label\">Read first</span></p>\n<p>Before this page: have you read <a data-wiki=\"Getting Started\" href=\"#/library/Getting_Started\">Getting Started</a>, <a data-wiki=\"Beginner Mistakes\" href=\"#/library/Beginner_Mistakes\">Beginner Mistakes</a> and some of the <a href=\"#/library?cat=OS_theory\">OS theory</a>?</p>\n</div>\n<p><span class=\"wk-rating\" data-level=\"1\">Difficulty: Beginner</span></p>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox\">\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-title\">\n<p><a data-wiki=\"Kernel\" href=\"#/library/Kernel\">Kernel Designs</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\">Models</span> <a data-wiki=\"Monolithic Kernel\" href=\"#/library/Monolithic_Kernel\">Monolithic Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Microkernel\" href=\"#/library/Microkernel\">Microkernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Hybrid Kernel\" href=\"#/library/Hybrid_Kernel\">Hybrid Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Exokernel\" href=\"#/library/Exokernel\">Exokernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Exokernel\" href=\"#/library/Exokernel/nanokernel_picokernel\">Nano/Picokernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Exokernel\" href=\"#/library/Exokernel/cache_kernel\">Cache Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Exokernel\" href=\"#/library/Exokernel/virtualizing_kernel\">Virtualizing Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Megalithic Kernel\" href=\"#/library/Megalithic_Kernel\">Megalithic Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Multikernel\" href=\"#/library/Multikernel\">Multikernel</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\">Other Concepts</span> <a data-wiki=\"Modular Kernel\" href=\"#/library/Modular_Kernel\">Modular Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Higher Half Kernel\" href=\"#/library/Higher_Half_Kernel\">Higher Half Kernel</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Creating a 64-bit kernel\" href=\"#/library/Creating_a_64_bit_kernel\">64-bit Kernel</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>In this tutorial, you will write a basic ARM kernel and boot it. You will target the ARM Versatile Express development board for the Cortex-A15.</p>\n<h2 id=\"rationale\">Rationale</h2>\n<h3 id=\"why_armv7_a\">Why ARMv7-A?</h3>\n<p>ARMv7 is likely the last purely 32-bit iteration of the ARM architecture, so processors based on it are likely to be supported the longest. The 'A' profile is targeted at complex computing devices like smartphones, and is therefore of the most interest to OS developers.</p>\n<h3 id=\"why_the_cortex_a15\">Why the Cortex-A15?</h3>\n<p>Largely because it's the most powerful ARMv7-A processor supported by QEMU, and it also has its own development board.</p>\n<h3 id=\"why_the_versatile_express\">Why the Versatile Express?</h3>\n<p>This board was designed by ARM Holdings as a prototyping board, so it makes sense to target a relatively neutral platform built with the Cortex-A15 in mind.</p>\n<h2 id=\"toolchain\">Toolchain</h2>\n<p>You will be using the <a class=\"ext wk-missing\" href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/GNU_Toolchain\" rel=\"noopener\">GNU Toolchain</a> for this, so go read <a data-wiki=\"GCC Cross-Compiler\" href=\"#/library/GCC_Cross_Compiler\">GCC Cross-Compiler</a> if you haven't already. The target platform is <code>arm-none-eabi</code>. You will need at least <a data-wiki=\"GAS\" href=\"#/library/GAS\">GAS</a>, <a data-wiki=\"GCC\" href=\"#/library/GCC\">GCC</a>, and <a data-wiki=\"LD\" href=\"#/library/LD\">LD</a>, but it is also suggested to have <a data-wiki=\"GDB\" href=\"#/library/GDB\">GDB</a>, <a class=\"ext wk-missing\" href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/Objcopy\" rel=\"noopener\">Objcopy</a>, and <a class=\"ext wk-missing\" href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/Objdump\" rel=\"noopener\">Objdump</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"code\">Code</h2>\n<p>_start.arm:</p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre class=\"sourceCode gnuassembler\"><code class=\"sourceCode gnuassembler\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><span class=\"kw\">.global</span> _start</span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"><span class=\"fu\">_start:</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-3\">    ldr <span class=\"kw\">sp</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"op\">=</span>STACK_TOP</span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-4\">    <span class=\"kw\">bl</span> start</span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"><span class=\"fu\">1:</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-6\">    b <span class=\"dv\">1</span>b</span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-7\"><span class=\"kw\">.size</span> _start<span class=\"op\">,</span> . <span class=\"op\">-</span> _start</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>start.c:</p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb2\"><pre class=\"sourceCode c\"><code class=\"sourceCode c\"><span id=\"cb2-1\"><span class=\"pp\">#include </span><span class=\"im\">&lt;stdint.h&gt;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-2\"><span class=\"pp\">#define UART0_BASE </span><span class=\"bn\">0x1c090000</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-3\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-4\"><span class=\"dt\">void</span> start<span class=\"op\">()</span> <span class=\"op\">{</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-5\">    <span class=\"op\">*(</span><span class=\"dt\">volatile</span> <span class=\"dt\">uint32_t</span> <span class=\"op\">*)(</span>UART0_BASE<span class=\"op\">)</span> <span class=\"op\">=</span> <span class=\"ch\">'A'</span><span class=\"op\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-6\"><span class=\"op\">}</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>linker.ld:</p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb3\"><pre class=\"sourceCode c\"><code class=\"sourceCode c\"><span id=\"cb3-1\">ENTRY<span class=\"op\">(</span>_start<span class=\"op\">)</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-2\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-3\">SECTIONS <span class=\"op\">{</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-4\">    <span class=\"co\">/* QEMU loads the kernel in Flash here. I strongly suggest you look at the</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-5\"><span class=\"co\">     * memory map provided in the CoreTile TRM (see below).</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-6\"><span class=\"co\">     */</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-7\">    <span class=\"op\">.</span> <span class=\"op\">=</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x80010000</span><span class=\"op\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-8\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-9\">    <span class=\"co\">/* Make sure our entry stub goes first */</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-10\">    <span class=\"op\">.</span>stub   <span class=\"op\">:</span> <span class=\"op\">{</span> _start<span class=\"op\">.</span>o<span class=\"op\">(.</span>text<span class=\"op\">)</span> <span class=\"op\">}</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-11\">    <span class=\"op\">.</span>text   <span class=\"op\">:</span> <span class=\"op\">{</span> <span class=\"op\">*(.</span>text<span class=\"op\">)</span> <span class=\"op\">}</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-12\">    <span class=\"op\">.</span>rodata <span class=\"op\">:</span> <span class=\"op\">{</span> <span class=\"op\">*(.</span>rodata<span class=\"op\">)</span> <span class=\"op\">}</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-13\">    <span class=\"op\">.</span>data   <span class=\"op\">:</span> <span class=\"op\">{</span> <span class=\"op\">*(.</span>data<span class=\"op\">)</span> <span class=\"op\">}</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-14\">    <span class=\"op\">.</span>bss    <span class=\"op\">:</span> <span class=\"op\">{</span> <span class=\"op\">*(.</span>bss COMMON<span class=\"op\">)</span> <span class=\"op\">}</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-15\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-16\">    STACK_BASE <span class=\"op\">=</span> <span class=\"op\">.;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-17\">    <span class=\"op\">.</span> <span class=\"op\">+=</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x10000</span><span class=\"op\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-18\">    STACK_TOP <span class=\"op\">=</span> <span class=\"op\">.;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-19\"><span class=\"op\">}</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"building_and_running\">Building and Running</h2>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb4\"><pre class=\"sourceCode bash\"><code class=\"sourceCode bash\"><span id=\"cb4-1\"><span class=\"ex\">arm-none-eabi-as</span> <span class=\"at\">-march</span><span class=\"op\">=</span>armv7-a <span class=\"at\">-mcpu</span><span class=\"op\">=</span>cortex-a15 _start.arm <span class=\"at\">-o</span> _start.o</span>\r\n<span id=\"cb4-2\"><span class=\"ex\">arm-none-eabi-gcc</span> <span class=\"at\">-ffreestanding</span> <span class=\"at\">-Wall</span> <span class=\"at\">-Wextra</span> <span class=\"at\">-Werror</span> <span class=\"at\">-c</span> start.c <span class=\"at\">-o</span> start.o</span>\r\n<span id=\"cb4-3\"><span class=\"ex\">arm-none-eabi-ld</span> <span class=\"at\">-T</span> linker.ld _start.o start.o <span class=\"at\">-o</span> kernel.elf</span>\r\n<span id=\"cb4-4\"><span class=\"ex\">qemu-system-arm</span> <span class=\"at\">-M</span> vexpress-a15 <span class=\"at\">-cpu</span> cortex-a15 <span class=\"at\">-kernel</span> kernel.elf <span class=\"at\">-nographic</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"see_also\">See Also</h2>\n<h3 id=\"external_links\">External Links</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://infocenter.arm.com/help/index.jsp?topic=/com.arm.doc.subset.boards.express/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\">ARMv7 Cortex-A Series Programmer's Guide</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://infocenter.arm.com/help/index.jsp?topic=/com.arm.doc.ddi0406c/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\">ARMv7-A Architecture Reference Manual</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://infocenter.arm.com/help/index.jsp?topic=/com.arm.doc.ddi0406c/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\">ARM Cortex-A15 Technical Reference Manual</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://infocenter.arm.com/help/index.jsp?topic=/com.arm.doc.subset.boards.express/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\">CoreTile Express A-15 Technical Reference Manual</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://infocenter.arm.com/help/index.jsp?topic=/com.arm.doc.subset.boards.express/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\">Motherboard Express μATX Technical Reference Manual</a></li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"rationale","text":"Rationale","level":2},{"id":"why_armv7_a","text":"Why ARMv7-A?","level":3},{"id":"why_the_cortex_a15","text":"Why the Cortex-A15?","level":3},{"id":"why_the_versatile_express","text":"Why the Versatile Express?","level":3},{"id":"toolchain","text":"Toolchain","level":2},{"id":"code","text":"Code","level":2},{"id":"building_and_running","text":"Building and Running","level":2},{"id":"see_also","text":"See Also","level":2},{"id":"external_links","text":"External Links","level":3}],"categories":["ARM","Bare bones tutorials"],"rating":1,"flags":[],"words":469,"summary":"In this tutorial, you will write a basic ARM kernel and boot it. You will target the ARM Versatile Express development board for the Cortex-A15.","updated":"2018-09-10","authors":["Carver"],"url":"https://wiki.osdev.org/ARMv7-A_Bare_Bones","history":"https://wiki.osdev.org/index.php?title=ARMv7-A_Bare_Bones&action=history","backlinks":[{"t":"Raspberry Pi Bare Bones","s":"Raspberry_Pi_Bare_Bones"}],"lessons":[{"id":"t15m3l2","title":"ARM and AArch64","kind":"further"}]}